> Start with source scores whose losses can be checked by hand

For separate real and fake logit pools, with sp the stable softplus,

\[L_D=\operatorname{mean}sp(-r)+\operatorname{mean}sp(f),\quad L_G=\operatorname{mean}sp(-f).\]

At scalar r=f=0, D=2log2 and G=log2. D derivatives are-σ(-r)/N andσ(f)/M;
G's fake-logit derivative is-σ(-f)/M. Thus when D confidently calls a generated
image fake, f=-80, the non-saturating G derivative remains near-1/M. Direct
softplus(-f) also avoids cancellation in softplus(f)-f. The reporting sigmoid
is explicit; fitting uses logits and stable softplus, never log of a rounded probability.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/conditional_gan_derivatives.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::vector<double> x, dr, df, gf;
  for (int k = -60; k <= 60; ++k) {
    x.push_back(k / 20.);
    auto r          = n::full({1, 1}, k / 20., n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_(),
         f          = n::full({1, 1}, k / 20., n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
    const auto loss = n::models::LogisticGanObjectives(r, f);
    const auto d    = n::grad(loss.discriminator, {r, f});
    dr.push_back(d[0].item());
    df.push_back(d[1].item());
    gf.push_back(n::grad(n::models::LogisticGanObjectives(r, f).generator, {f})[0].item());
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines(x, dr, "D real derivative", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .lines(x, df, "D fake derivative", {22, 163, 74}, 2.)
      .lines(x, gf, "G fake derivative", {220, 38, 38}, 2.)
      .y_limits(-1.25, 1.5)
      .x_label("Respective scalar raw source score")
      .y_label("Derivative; each pool size1")
      .title("Logistic objective: distinguish D and G directions")
      .save_svg("build/conditional_gan_derivatives.svg");
  auto r          = n::zeros({1, 1}, n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_(),
       f          = n::zeros({1, 1}, n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
  const auto loss = n::models::LogisticGanObjectives(r, f);
  const auto d    = n::grad(loss.discriminator, {r, f});
  const auto g    = n::grad(n::models::LogisticGanObjectives(r, f).generator, {f});
  std::print(
      "Hand-check: D={:.9f},G={:.9f}; D derivatives={},{}; G derivative={}.\n",
      loss.discriminator.item(),
      loss.generator.item(),
      d[0].item(),
      d[1].item(),
      g[0].item());
}
```
