> One-hot conditioning can be traced with one hidden unit

Take two classes, one noise coordinate z=0 and one real pixel x=.25. Class0 has
one-hot(1,0), class 1 has(0,1). Set all biases to zero, both output weights to one,
G's hidden weights on(z,c0,c1) to(0,0,1), and D's on(x,c0,c1) to(1,0,2).
Then G produces sigmoid(tanh(c1)): .5 or about .6817. On the same real pixel,
D returns tanh(.25+2c1): about .2449 or .9780. Thus class enters each network
before its nonlinearity; no class target or classifier head supplies these outputs.
The two plotted outputs have different meanings: bounded G pixel and raw D score.
Their common numerical range here does not make the D score a probability.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/conditional_gan_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n         = dm::nn;
  namespace m         = n::models;
  const auto        t = n::DType::Float64;
  n::ParameterStore g(1, t), d(2, t);
  auto              z = n::zeros({2, 1}, t), x = n::full({2, 1}, .25, t);
  auto              labels = n::tensor({0, 1}, {2}, n::DType::Int64);
  {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    m::ConditionalGan(g, d, x, z, labels, 1, 2, 1);
  }
  g.set("hidden/W", n::tensor({0, 0, 1}, {3, 1}, t));
  g.set("output/W", n::ones({1, 1}, t));
  d.set("hidden/W", n::tensor({1, 0, 2}, {3, 1}, t));
  d.set("output/W", n::ones({1, 1}, t));
  const auto out = m::ConditionalGan(g, d, x, z, labels, 1, 2, 1);
  std::print(
      "| class | one-hot | G pixel | D real raw score "
      "|\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n|0|1,0|{:.9f}|{:.9f}|\n|1|0,1|{:.9f}|{:.9f}|\n",
      out.fake.at({0, 0}),
      out.real_logit.at({0, 0}),
      out.fake.at({1, 0}),
      out.real_logit.at({1, 0}));
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.points({0, 1}, out.fake.to_vector<double>(), "G sigmoid pixel", {37, 99, 235}, 6.)
      .points({0, 1}, out.real_logit.to_vector<double>(), "D real raw score", {220, 38, 38}, 6.)
      .x_limits(-.4, 1.4)
      .y_limits(0, 1.5)
      .x_label("Supplied class0 or1; same z0 and real pixel0.25")
      .y_label("Different output meanings: pixel and raw score")
      .title("One-hot inputs change both small networks")
      .save_svg("build/conditional_gan_toy.svg");
}
