> The coarse diagnostic has a deliberately visible blind spot

The MMD diagnostic first averages each 7×7 pixel block, giving16 coordinates per image,
and divides those coordinates by4. It then averages IMQ kernels with constants1,4,16
and excludes within-pool diagonals in the unbiased two-sample estimate. This statistic
can be negative at finite sample size and discards fine digit structure. The baseline
repeats the fitting-only mean image200 times; it uses no held-out pixels to construct it.
Its much smaller value shows why coarse MMD alone cannot certify sample quality or
coverage. Neither the mean nor MMD adds a fitting objective or selects the checkpoint.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/conditional_gan_mean.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
