> A shared noise bank exposes the class condition

The same ten test noise vectors are repeated for every requested class. Row c supplies
class c to G; columns retain noise identity. Changing the class changes a generated pixel
by at most0.068083525; shifting each real image's
class by one changes a real D logit by at most0.202480078.
These are structural dependence controls. The weak gallery does not show that requested
digits are recognizable. No auxiliary classifier is fitted, so no class accuracy is invented.
Negative, out-of-range and mismatched labels are all rejected before one-hot expansion.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/conditional_gan_classes.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
