> Verification and limits

The unchanged original delegated to the new core, and this complete report, each match
all 8 archives/845165 values exactly in dtype, shape and value bytes,
the history and batch TSVs, all 3 source PNGs and every non-timing JSON value. Duration is
remeasured. Native source snapshots and checksums retain the frozen baseline.

The independent NumPy checker imports no datamunge and performs no fitting. It checks
732625 forward/control values, every one of the52209 initial parameter derivatives,
22 scalar finite differences and all 3000 fitting-row visits. It includes stable extreme-logit derivatives and both class/noise controls.
Component checks separately exercise owned records, malformed inputs, live continuous
paths and D-then-fresh-G ownership in native C++, Python and R. Those component checks
do not complete independent Python/R experiment loops.

This is one fixed short run, with no seed sweep, uncertainty estimate or paper-scale
image benchmark. The training schedule and width are intentionally preserved. The result
illustrates conditioning and stable logistic objectives; it supplies no evidence that this small game has converged.
The weak samples and strong constant-baseline MMD remain part of the explanation.

Method reference: [Mirza and Osindero, Conditional Generative Adversarial Nets (2014)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.1784). Seeds, dimensions, source IDs, update order and artifacts follow
the original repository experiment. Canonical native tensor maps, stable losses, seeded
Gaussian generation and IMQ diagnostics provide the reusable computations.
